(`Free` through one of two parameters naming one list empties it under
 both names, and the caller's, and a later write through the other is
 refused with the error flag (docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #140).)
To 'merge' of a list called first and a list called second.
    Free first.
    Print "second sees: {second's length}".
    append "after" to second.
    On error print "the append was refused".
    Print "second now: {second}".

a list called xs is ["a", "b"].
'merge' of xs and xs.
Print "xs: {xs}".
